[SPEAKER_01]: systems have been coming or the flying conditions have been evolving over the past period of 20 years, like what you looked at? in the

15:53.987 --> 16:04.555
[SPEAKER_01]: beginning, how it was back in 2000s and what is it now after a couple of decades? Yeah, I do genuinely think that the seasons are getting later.

16:05.075 --> 16:15.484
[SPEAKER_00]: And I would say, yeah, the rainy season has been pushed back. When I first came, late September was good. And now it seems to be more like from the

16:15.524 --> 16:27.936
[SPEAKER_00]: 10th of October. I see. When it comes to glider handling or any of those things in the condition, has that evolved over a period of time that now

16:27.956 --> 16:39.606
[SPEAKER_01]: you need to handle it a bit more or the air is a bit more rougher and the systems have to work a bit more harder than what you used to earlier with

16:39.866 --> 16:48.592
[SPEAKER_01]: the change in climate and weather systems? Well, no, my experience, but this is very anecdotal. I haven't sort of looked at this statistically.

16:49.033 --> 16:58.420
[SPEAKER_00]: Beer, you know, it's a short season, isn't it? Between the too much stability of the instability in the monsoon to then it becoming too

16:58.460 --> 17:08.848
